   "evidence": "Mathlib/Analysis/MellinTransform.lean:45 `def MellinConvergent (f : \u211d \u2192 E) (s : \u2102) : Prop := IntegrableOn \u2026`; Mathlib itself always unfolds it by name \u2014 line 72 `rw [MellinConvergent, MellinConvergent, \u2026]`, line 78 `rw [MellinConvergent]`, line 444 `simp_rw [HasMellin, mellin, MellinConvergent, \u2026]`. No `MellinConvergent.mono_set` or `MellinConvergent.of_forall_sdiff_eq_zero` exists (grep of MellinTransform.lean lines 45-80 lists every `MellinConvergent.*` lemma: `const_smul`, `cpow_smul`, `div_const`, `comp_mul_left`, `comp_rpow`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Convolution/Strip.lean",
   "fix": "Make the unfolding explicit, as Mathlib does in this file: add `MellinConvergent` to the opening `rw`/`simp_rw` list (`rw [mellinDisConvergent_def, MellinConvergent, integrableOn_congr_fun \u2026]`), so both `.of_forall_sdiff_eq_zero` and `.mono_set` act on a visible `IntegrableOn` goal/hypothesis.",
   "issue": "Both directions silently unfold Mathlib's `def MellinConvergent`: `h.of_forall_sdiff_eq_zero` produces an `IntegrableOn` term for a `MellinConvergent` goal, and `h.mono_set` resolves dot notation on a `MellinConvergent` hypothesis only because Lean whnf's the def away. Nothing in the proof records that this step is a defeq crossing, and the PR adds `mellinDisConvergent_def` precisely to avoid this pattern for its own definition.",
   "line": 177
  }
